WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.886
(crinkling)

00:00:00.886 --> 00:00:03.661
- People have told me I
have saved their life.

00:00:03.661 --> 00:00:05.624
(crunching)

00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:09.138
I became a ASMR artist on YouTube.

00:00:09.138 --> 00:00:10.857
(crunching)

00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:14.722
Because I deal with my own pain each day.

00:00:14.722 --> 00:00:16.776
(tapping)

00:00:16.776 --> 00:00:20.047
ASMR has truly helped me focus on living

00:00:20.047 --> 00:00:21.775
instead of dying.

00:00:21.775 --> 00:00:23.084
Close your eyes.

00:00:23.084 --> 00:00:25.251
(tapping)

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.568
(shaking)

00:00:29.568 --> 00:00:30.401
(crunching)

00:00:30.401 --> 00:00:33.901
An ASMR artist is someone who focus mainly

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.933
on visual triggers and sounds to bring you

00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:39.933
some type of relaxation.

00:00:42.416 --> 00:00:45.416
Some of the misconceptions
that people have with ASMR

00:00:45.416 --> 00:00:49.999
is thinking that it's creepy,
it's cringey, it's weird,

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.227
and I believe the reason
why some people believe that

00:00:55.227 --> 00:00:58.594
ASMR is so weird is because
I'm constantly whispering.

00:00:58.594 --> 00:01:02.740
I'm going to take a sip of
my hot coffee for a second.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.806
But when ASMR artists' whisper,

00:01:05.806 --> 00:01:08.651
it's to bring you to that safe place.

00:01:08.651 --> 00:01:10.847
It's to make you feel calm.

00:01:10.847 --> 00:01:14.107
Tell yourself, “You're going to be okay."

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:17.082
I find my sounds in any
and everything that I do.

00:01:17.082 --> 00:01:19.868
(crinkling)

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:23.531
If I'm opening up a pack of
gum, if I'm brushing my hair,

00:01:23.531 --> 00:01:27.263
people love crunch sounds
like the pickle video.

00:01:27.263 --> 00:01:28.180
I'll snack.

00:01:29.112 --> 00:01:30.308
(crunching)

00:01:30.308 --> 00:01:31.933
I don't know what happens.

00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:35.162
Why does eating a pickle
causes a person's brain

00:01:35.162 --> 00:01:37.381
to shut down, but it will.

00:01:37.381 --> 00:01:39.861
(crunch)

00:01:39.861 --> 00:01:40.694
Wow. Yeah.

00:01:42.827 --> 00:01:45.575
I have a degenerative bone disease.

00:01:45.575 --> 00:01:47.757
I can't stop it, there's no cure.

00:01:47.757 --> 00:01:51.792
Before I discovered
ASMR, I could not move.

00:01:51.792 --> 00:01:55.683
I didn't have the strength
to make myself stand up.

00:01:55.683 --> 00:02:00.683
So, when I discovered ASMR,
I felt extremely relaxed.

00:02:00.806 --> 00:02:04.337
I feel like I was actually
smiling just laying there.

00:02:04.337 --> 00:02:06.412
I felt really, really good mentally.

00:02:06.412 --> 00:02:08.653
More so than being on medication.

00:02:08.653 --> 00:02:11.661
And I said, “Okay, I'm
going to create a channel,

00:02:11.661 --> 00:02:14.809
and I'm going to create
ASMR videos because there's

00:02:14.809 --> 00:02:17.892
a lot of people who are
dealing with stress, insomnia,

00:02:17.892 --> 00:02:20.466
anxiety; who just need some comfort

00:02:20.466 --> 00:02:22.865
to get them through the night."

00:02:22.865 --> 00:02:26.573
I receive email from
people who are bed ridden

00:02:26.573 --> 00:02:29.977
and let me know how
much I have helped them.

00:02:29.977 --> 00:02:31.760
I always told my children

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.793
one person could change the world.

00:02:33.793 --> 00:02:38.650
And to actually be a part
of maybe some type of change

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.317
in some type of way, is amazing.

